Author: hkjang <gagagiga@naver.com>
Date:   Thu Sep 17 22:02:26 2026 +0900

    build(web): accept a forwarded --silent in the typecheck and build scripts

    npm consumes --silent in 'npm run typecheck --silent', but pnpm forwards it
    to the script line, where tsc (TS5072) and vite (CACError) reject it as an
    unknown option. Automated verification runners rely on the npm convention,
    so route the two scripts through scripts/run-tool.mjs, which resolves the
    tool through its package manifest and drops only trailing quiet flags. The
    checks themselves are unchanged; a node:test file covers the flag handling,
    bin resolution, and exit-status passthrough.

